::MCR_U03_L07_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U03_L07_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.DL.7
Question:
Which response best supports this statistical report skill: interpret a two-way table?
{
=A. Use the table, display, sample, and claim together before writing a conclusion.#Correct. A responsible report interpretation checks evidence, context, sample, and limits.
~B. Accept the headline without checking the data.#Headlines can overstate data, so the evidence must be checked.
~C. Use only the largest number in the report.#One number is not enough to evaluate a full statistical report.
~D. Ignore who was sampled.#The sample affects whether the conclusion can generalize.
}


